event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":362,"item_id":"fc_01b0d51061bf793d016adf2b87fac48191860785032e42c303","output_index":0,"arguments":"{\"pointer\":\"/checks/complete_target_and_representations\",\"coverage\":\"assessed\",\"judgment\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Independently verified the equivalent coordinate encoding against source-context definitions and Proof.lean lines 7–44, 575–602. H001 excludes zero dimensions; Fin n merely reindexes the n standard directions. The auxiliary spatial sup norm induces the same topology and differential structure as Euclidean coordinates, while every norm in sphere constraints and density is genuinely Euclidean in Y m. Product real volume is standard Lebesgue measure. Extension of u to nonpositive times is unrestricted, since dom is open t>0 and all iterated derivatives there depend only on its germ. Pointwise scalars need no smooth selection; slab support is support of u−q, not of u, with no global-in-time compact set demanded. dx is the coordinate directional Fréchet derivative, equal to the source partial under joint smoothness. Laplacian and Frobenius square use exactly these directions. Integrable real sections guard the finite energy integral; DifferentiableOn on the open half-line and ordinary deriv=0 retain both existence and zero derivative, followed by equality for all positive times, including either ordering and equality. No target clause is omitted. Local predicates contain substantive proof fields but are discharged internally, not exported assumptions. Actual derivative-view and coordinate-slicing conversions are supplied in T002 and T010–T011; no unimplemented second model is relied upon.\",\"locations\":[\"/scope\",\"/endpoints\",\"/mechanical_summary\",\"/scope/full_target\",\"/scope/parameters\",\"/scope/hypotheses\",\"/endpoints/P/source\",\"/endpoints/P/actual\",\"/endpoints/P/correspondence\",\"/documents\"]}}"}

